summary: selinux-testsuite on MLS enforcing with COPR selinux-policy-mls
description: |
    Install selinux-policy-mls from Packit COPR for selinux-policy PR
    ${PR_NUMBER} (packit/fedora-selinux-selinux-policy-${PR_NUMBER}), switch
    the guest to MLS enforcing, run upstream selinux-testsuite unmodified.

    Set PR_NUMBER via environment (default 3380). Pin uses repo-scoped NVR
    query so dnf does not pick a newer build from Fedora repos. Prefer
    compose Fedora-44 when validating a PR built for that chroot.

    Policy fixes (cloud-init, udev, ssh pipes, semanage/checkpolicy under
    MLS, etc.) must be in the COPR RPM — no guest-local semodule build.

    Excludes upstream tests incompatible with this MLS guest:
    /prepare-system$ (redundant third reboot; our prepare sets sysadm_u and
    ssh_sysadm_login), /unprepare$ (tries unconfined_u on MLS).

environment:
  PR_NUMBER: "3380"
  STS_ROOT_DOMAIN: sysadm_t
  STS_KERNEL: local

prepare:
  - name: COPR selinux-policy-mls, MLS switch, enforcing (2 reboots)
    how: shell
    script: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-final-copr-prepare.sh

discover:
  - name: selinux-testsuite
    how: fmf
    url: https://github.com/SELinuxProject/selinux-testsuite
    ref: main
    filter: tag:-ci & tag:-nfs
    exclude:
      - /prepare-system$
      - /unprepare$

execute:
  how: tmt
